dence_ids":["link.quartic.proposition-3"],"id":"quartic.proposition-3","kind":"claim","label":"Proposition 3","locator":"Proposition 3, Section 4.2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Proposition 3** (OpenAI ([OpenAI 2026](#cite-OpenAI2026), Proposition 3.2)). *Let $T=\\lceil\\log(1000m)\\rceil$ and $\\varepsilon=1/(1000T)$. Suppose a reversible comparison circuit, controlled by two candidate indices, uses at most $c$ queries and satisfies (4). There is a quantum algorithm making $O(c\\sqrt m\\,T^2\\log T)$ queries on every branch and returning a list of at most $T$ candidates such that, if $a_{i^\\star j}\\ge1-\\varepsilon$ for all $j\\ne i^\\star$, the list contains $i^\\star$ with probability at least $1-2m2^{-T}-T\\varepsilon$.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:64b4bff49f4a37d69616e0b90f4914305cfb20c7c3287b1bc972500c7b211f5d/nodes/quartic.proposition-3","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:64b4bff49f4a37d69616e0b90f4914305cfb20c7c3287b1bc972500c7b211f5d/nodes/quartic.proposition-3","id":"sha256:64b4bff49f4a37d69616e0b90f4914305cfb20c7c3287b1bc972500c7b211f5d/edges/%5B%22quartic.proposition-3%22%2C%22lean.QuarticQuery.Paper.quantumTournament%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:64b4bff49f4a37d69616e0b90f4914305cfb20c7c3287b1bc972500c7b211f5d/edges/%5B%22quartic.proposition-3%22%2C%22lean.QuarticQuery.Paper.quantumTournament%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:64b4bff49f4a37d69616e0b90f4914305cfb20c7c3287b1bc972500c7b211f5d/nodes/lean.QuarticQuery.Paper.quantumTournament"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:64b4bff49f4a37d69616e0b90f4914305cfb20c7c3287b1bc972500c7b211f5d/evidence/link.quartic.proposition-3","id":"field:3629ce91fe44efc88d0bbe8bf768773692480240c1b363c4da78d8b25101c1f7","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:64b4bff49f4a37d69616e0b90f4914305cfb20c7c3287b1bc972500c7b211f5d/evidence/link.quartic.proposition-3","semantic